id: pm-glmcnd
title: Release publication downloads the producer-binding artifact once and blocks the daily cut when the download endpoint trails the listing
description: "The blocker_retry Auto Release run 45818705282 on 2026-11-26 passed every gate, uploaded release-producer-binding-1 (artifact 15118638954, finalized 12:56:28.2Z), found it in a complete inventory on the first read, and failed 1.5 s later in recordReleasePublicationOrigin: gh run download returned HTTP 404 for actions/artifacts/15118638954/zip. Nothing was pushed or published and blocker issue GH-1788 was reopened with a retry marker, so only a manual dispatch could still cut the day's release. pm-jvb9pk made the inventory read wait out a trailing listing; the download of a listed artifact is a second read of the same eventually consistent store and still runs once, so a not-yet-servable archive costs the whole daily release exactly as a trailing listing did."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:release",auto-release,"gh:1788",reliability
